  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "THE COMPLEX VOLUME OF SL(n, C)-REPRESENTATIONS OF 3-MANIFOLDS — For a compact 3-manifold M with arbitrary (possibly empty) boundary, we give a parametrization of the set of conjugacy classes of\n\n**THE COMPLEX VOLUME OF SL(n, C)-REPRESENTATIONS OF 3-MANIFOLDS**\n\n*STAVROS GAROUFALIDIS, DYLAN P. THURSTON, AND CHRISTIAN K. ZICKERT*\n\n44 pp, 31 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** For a compact 3-manifold M with arbitrary (possibly empty) boundary, we give a parametrization of the set of conjugacy classes of boundary-unipotent representations of π1(M) into SL(n, C). Our parametrization uses Ptolemy coordinates, which are inspired by coordinates on higher Teichmüller spaces due to Fock and Goncharov. We show that a boundary-unipotent representation determines an element in Neumann’s extended Bloch group bB(C), and use this to obtain an eﬃcient formula for the Cheeger-Chern-Simons invariant, and in particular for the vol- ume. Computations for the census manifolds show that boundary-unipotent representations are abundant, and numerical comparisons with census volumes, suggest that the volume of a represen- tation is an integral linear combination of volumes of hyperbolic 3-manifolds.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Statement of our results; 1.3 Overview of the paper; 1.4 Acknowledgment; 2 The Cheeger-Chern-Simons classes; 2.1 Simply connected, simple Lie groups; 2.2 Complex groups and volume; 2.3 The universal classes and group cohomology; 2.4 Compact manifolds with boundary; 2.5 Central elements of order 2; 3 The extended Bloch group; 3.1 The regulator; 3.3 Arbitrary fields; 4 Decorations of representations; 4.1 The fundamental class of a decorated repre; 5 Generic decorations and Ptolemy coordinates; 5.1 The geometry of the Ptolemy coordinates",
      "lang": "en",
